### Shared validation implementation checkpoint, 2026-09-29

The main agent's subsequent continuation message explicitly confirmed the genuine RED and 29 unchanged inputs and authorized minimal production implementation. That authorization supersedes the preceding local implementation hold; it does not authorize a commit/push, ledger/status change or formal gate verdict. `validation-red-20260929-01a0ebb9/root-confirmation.json` records the received authority and binds the exact inspected hashes. It is a message-confirmed local checkpoint, not a new ledger reservation or Git receipt.

#### Root cause and minimal change

Separate `parseJson` and `redact` helpers existed, but no common entrance checked the closed schema and trusted ownership/path/Git conditions before returning a redacted preparation. The only new production file is `plugins/sdd-context/validation.mjs` (198 lines), exporting one `validate` function. It reuses those helpers, Node built-ins and the actual imported `$defs.taskEntry`; it adds no dependency, parser, MCP startup, journal or native adapter.

The shared flow is raw JSON admission → closed schema/owner checks → canonical worktree/Git-directory and planned path checks → effective ignore/untracked checks → redaction under the same original trusted monotonic deadline → path recheck → in-memory return. Existing target files are opened read-only and checked against their filesystem identity; this function never creates or writes a store. Failures discard underlying exceptions and expose only `validation-rejected`, without stack, cause, content or returned value. A future writer must revalidate immediately at actual use; this preparation is not a write capability or a claim of durability.

